# Expense report

The user gives the receipts folder and the month. The result is `report.md`
in the receipts folder.

## Rules

- Never write `report.md` before the user approves the table.
- Never change or move a receipt file.
- Never go on without receipts: `scripts/scan.sh` stops the run when the
  folder has none for the month.
- Amounts in the report have two decimals and the currency code.

## S1 — Scan the receipts

Run `scripts/scan.sh <folder> <month>`. It prints one line per receipt: file,
date, amount, currency. When the folder has no receipts for the month, the
script exits 1: tell the user that the folder has no receipts and stop.

## S2 — Categorize

Give each receipt one category: travel, meals, office, or other. The match
words are in [categories.md](references/categories.md). Report a receipt
that has no amount.

When any receipt is in a foreign currency, ask the user for the exchange rate
of each foreign currency.

## S3 — Review

Show the receipts with their categories and the total of each category. Ask
the user to approve the table. Apply the corrections that the user gives and
show the table again. When the user does not want a report, stop.

## S4 — Write the report

Run `scripts/write-report.sh <folder>` with the approved table on standard
input. It writes `report.md` in the receipts folder.

Then tell the user the path of the report and the grand total in one line.
